abstract: >
  MOLEKUL is a notebook-based teaching platform for ab initio quantum chemistry.
  It pairs a pure-Python library (NumPy core, SciPy for geometry optimization)
  with a 14-notebook curriculum covering RHF, UHF, MP2, CCSD, CCSD(T),
  KS-DFT, CIS, TD-DFT/TDA, EOM-CCSD, gradients, population analysis,
  and model periodic systems with phonons. Results are validated against
  PySCF. The code is designed for students who want to step through the
  implementation of quantum-chemical methods, not for production calculations.
